  "title": "Signed bits see one bit of the linking form",
  "subject": "What signed one-bit edge laws detect of a closed orientable three-manifold",
  "conclusion": "The twisted laws compute the Gauss sum of the cubic form a -> a^3 on H^1(M; Z/2), which is linear, so they see exactly whether the linking form gives 1/2 on an element of order 2. That bit is not a function of homology: it separates RP^3 # RP^3 from S^3/Q_8 and sampled triangulations that every counting law identifies.",
